# Temporary Android 17 bring-up probe. Delete once the boot hang is understood.
#
# post-fs-data in system/etc/init/hw/init.rc does:
#
#     restorecon /data/media
#     start casefolding_remover
#     wait_for_prop ro.casefolding.adjusted 1
#
# wait_for_prop has no timeout. /system/bin/casefolding_remover drives the
# FS_CASEFOLD_FL ioctl on /data/media, and 4.9 has no casefolding support at
# all: no CONFIG_UNICODE, and neither ext4 nor f2fs grew the flag before 5.2
# and 5.4. If the tool errors out instead of reporting nothing to do, it never
# sets the property and init blocks in post-fs-data for ever. No zygote, no
# boot animation, the bootloader splash stays on screen and only recovery is
# reachable. Android 16 ran the same operation as a plain exec whose failure
# was ignored, which is why it boots.
#
# Claiming the property first makes that wait return immediately. It is
# read-only, so the first writer wins.
#
# post-fs is the trigger immediately before post-fs-data and runs well after
# every /vendor/etc/init file has been parsed, so the ordering is safe.
#
# Caveat: plat_sepolicy grants set on casefolding_status_prop only to the
# casefolding_remover domain, so this needs a permissive build to take effect.
# It is a diagnostic, not a fix.

on post-fs
    setprop ro.casefolding.adjusted 1
